{"id":"decision-example-001","type":"decision","fact":"Example: Chose Zustand over Redux for client state management because of simpler API and smaller bundle size.","recommendation":"Use Zustand stores for client state. Use TanStack Query for server state. Do not mix the two patterns.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"Architecture decision","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["architecture","state-management","zustand"],"affectedFiles":["src/stores/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"decision-proxy-container-name","type":"decision","fact":"The proxy container is identified by a fixed Docker name (easy-proxy), queried via 'docker ps -f name=^easy-proxy$'. Docker is the single source of truth - no state file.","recommendation":"Address the container by name (EASY_PROXY_NAME) in proxy.sh. Do not reintroduce a state file to track the container id.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"Architectural decision - issue #5","date":"2026-05-18"}],"tags":["architecture","docker","proxy"],"affectedFiles":["commands/proxy.sh"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-18T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"decision-bats-test-gate","type":"decision","fact":"The pre-push and task-completion gate runs 'bats test/' (fast pass/fail). kcov coverage is informational only - instrumenting bats with kcov takes 7+ minutes, too slow to gate.","recommendation":"Keep enforcement.command in .coverage-thresholds.json as 'bats test/'. Run 'kcov coverage bats test/' manually for a coverage report; never wire kcov into CI or hooks.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"discovered building the test harness, issue #7","date":"2026-05-18"}],"tags":["testing","coverage","kcov","bats","ci"],"affectedFiles":[".coverage-thresholds.json",".husky/pre-push"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-18T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-18T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "decision-avoid-wildcard-without-dns-plugin", "type": "decision", "fact": "A wildcard certificate can only be validated by DNS-01; HTTP-01 cannot issue wildcards. That makes the wildcard choice a hard constraint on the DNS provider: it is sustainable only where a certbot DNS plugin exists (IONOS, Route53, Cloudflare, DigitalOcean are installed in the image). With a provider that has no plugin (e.g. Aruba) a wildcard means manual renewals forever - which is exactly how a production cert silently expired and went six months unnoticed.", "recommendation": "Default to a non-wildcard cert covering apex plus the few names actually used, validated by HTTP-01 webroot - it auto-renews with no dependency on the DNS provider's API. Caveat: /var/www/certbot is only an anonymous VOLUME declared in the Dockerfile (not bind-mounted by easy proxy create) and no template serves /.well-known/acme-challenge/, so the port-80 vhost needs 'location ^~ /.well-known/acme-challenge/ { root /var/www/certbot; }' (and any HTTP->HTTPS redirect must exclude that path). Choose a wildcard only when the DNS zone sits with a plugin-supported provider. If a wildcard is genuinely required on an unsupported provider: either move the zone's nameservers to a supported provider (registrar can stay), or delegate once by hand with CNAME _acme-challenge.<domain> -> _acme-challenge.<name>.<controlled-zone>. The delegation does NOT work with certbot-dns-ionos directly: the plugin picks the IONOS zone by suffix-matching the certificate domain (_find_managed_zone_id) and never follows CNAMEs, so it fails with zone-not-found; it needs a --manual-auth-hook script that writes the TXT to the delegated name via the IONOS API (or acme.sh --challenge-alias). acme.sh dns_aruba exists but targets the Aruba Business (reseller) API, not standard aruba.it customer accounts.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "production session production: first working IONOS DNS-01 integration + auto-renewal", "date": "2026-09-09"}, {"source": "agent", "reference": "verified certbot-dns-ionos source + Dockerfile/create mounts", "date": "2026-09-10"}], "tags": ["letsencrypt", "dns-01", "http-01", "wildcard", "certbot", "architecture"], "affectedFiles": ["commands/proxy.sh", "Dockerfile"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
